<description>
Extend the edge-touching green start bar through the corridor, turning at each teal blocker until the path leaves the grid.

Input structure:
- The background is the most common color.
- Exactly two foreground colors are present: a 2-pixel 4-connected start bar and many blocker pixels.
- Exactly one pixel of the start bar lies on the grid border.

Rule:
- Start from the border pixel of the bar and move through the other bar pixel into the grid.
- Paint every traversed non-blocker pixel with the start color.
- When the next cell is a blocker, turn to the unique perpendicular non-blocker neighbor; when the next cell is outside the grid, stop.

Key insight: The blocker pixels define a one-cell-wide corridor, so every interior collision has exactly one valid 90-degree turn.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "2-pixel start bar with one endpoint on the grid border",
  "path": "continue from the border endpoint through the other endpoint; move straight through non-blocker cells, turn at each blocker to the unique perpendicular non-blocker neighbor, and stop when the next step would leave the grid",
  "trajectory": "paint every visited non-blocker pixel with the start-bar color",
  "transform": "keep blocker pixels and existing start pixels unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  type: move_along_path
  grid: 5-8 rows x 5-8 cols [observed]
  colors:
    bg: most common color (always 7/orange [observed])
    path_color: exactly 2 pixels in input (always 3/green [observed])
    blocker_color: 6-14 pixels in input (always 8/azure [observed])
  start_bar:
    shape: 2-pixel 4-connected bar
    placement: one pixel on grid border, one pixel inward (perpendicular to border edge)
    entry_side: any of top/bottom/left/right
  blockers:
    count: 6-14 (scales ~0.20-0.24 of grid area)
    role: each turn requires 2 blockers -- one ahead (stops forward) + one on wrong perpendicular side (forces unique turn)
    extra: 0-2 distractor blockers not adjacent to path allowed [observed]
    isolation: mostly isolated (no 4-adjacent pair), but occasional adjacency OK
  path:
    trajectory: starts at inner bar pixel moving inward; goes straight until hitting blocker then turns 90deg to unique free perpendicular; stops when next step exits grid
    turns: 3-7
    segment_lengths: 1-5 cells per straight segment
    total_new_cells: 9-22
    self_crossing: path may revisit adjacent cells at tight U-turns (train_0/train_1 have 4-neighbor path cells)
    exit: path exits through any grid border (need not match entry border)

generation_strategy:
  approach: path-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size (5-8 x 5-8) and 3 colors (bg, path_color, blocker_color).
    2. Fill grid with bg. Pick entry border side and position for the 2-pixel start bar.
    3. Simulate the path from the inner bar pixel inward. At each step, decide randomly whether to continue straight (1-5 cells) or place a turn. For a turn, place the ahead-blocker and wrong-side-blocker, then change direction 90deg. Ensure the wrong-side cell is either OOB or has a blocker.
    4. After 3-7 turns, let the final segment run until it exits the grid.
    5. Validate each turn has exactly 1 valid perpendicular choice (no ambiguous turns).
    6. Optionally scatter 0-2 extra distractor blockers on bg cells not adjacent to path.
    7. The input is the grid with only the 2-pixel start bar and blockers (erase the traced path to bg). Output is the fully traced path.
```
